msgid ":ref:`faq_cpu_count`"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:185
msgid ""
"Return various CPU statistics. All fields are :term:`cumulative counters "
"<cumulative counter>` since boot."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:188
msgid ""
":field:`ctx_switches`: number of :term:`context switches <context switch>` "
"(voluntary + involuntary)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:190
msgid ""
":field:`interrupts`: number of :term:`hardware interrupts <hardware "
"interrupt>`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:192
msgid ""
":field:`soft_interrupts`: number of :term:`soft interrupts <soft "
"interrupt>`; always set to ``0`` on Windows and SunOS."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:195
msgid ""
":field:`syscalls`: number of system calls; always set to ``0`` on Linux."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:197
msgid ""
">>> import psutil\n"
">>> psutil.cpu_stats()\n"
"scpustats(ctx_switches=20455687, interrupts=6598984, "
"soft_interrupts=2134212, syscalls=0)"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:207
msgid ""
"Return :field:`current`, :field:`min` and :field:`max` CPU frequencies "
"expressed in MHz. On Linux, :field:`current` is the real-time frequency "
"value (changing), on all other platforms this usually represents the nominal "
"\"fixed\" value (never changing)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:212
msgid ""
"If *percpu* is ``True``, and the system supports per-CPU frequency retrieval "
"(Linux and FreeBSD), a list of frequencies is returned for each CPU; if not, "
"a list with a single element is returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:216
msgid ""
"If :field:`min` and :field:`max` cannot be determined they are set to "
"``0.0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:219
msgid ""
"On some systems the CPU frequency cannot be determined at all (e.g. certain "
"virtual machines, containers or CPU architectures). In that case this "
"returns ``None``, or an empty list if *percpu* is ``True``. This can happen "
"on Linux, macOS and FreeBSD; on Windows and OpenBSD a value is always "
"returned."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:224
msgid ""
">>> import psutil\n"
">>> psutil.cpu_freq()\n"
"scpufreq(current=931.42925, min=800.0, max=3500.0)\n"
">>> psutil.cpu_freq(percpu=True)\n"
"[scpufreq(current=2394.945, min=800.0, max=3500.0),\n"
" scpufreq(current=2236.812, min=800.0, max=3500.0),\n"
" scpufreq(current=1703.609, min=800.0, max=3500.0),\n"
" scpufreq(current=1754.289, min=800.0, max=3500.0)]"
msgstr ""

