#: ../../../api.rst:435
msgid "Return system :term:`swap memory` statistics:"
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:437
msgid ""
":field:`total`: total swap space. On Windows this is derived as "
"``CommitLimit - PhysicalTotal``, representing virtual memory backed by the "
"page file rather than the raw page-file size."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:440
msgid ":field:`used`: swap space currently in use."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:441
msgid ":field:`free`: swap space not in use (``total - used``)."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:442
msgid ""
":field:`percent`: swap usage as a percentage, calculated as ``used / total * "
"100``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:444
msgid ""
":field:`sin`: number of bytes the system has moved from disk (:term:`swap "
"<swap memory>`) back into RAM. See :term:`swap-in`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:446
msgid ""
":field:`sout`: number of bytes the system has moved from RAM to disk (:term:"
"`swap <swap memory>`). A continuously increasing :field:`sout` rate is a "
"sign of memory pressure. See :term:`swap-out`."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:450
msgid ""
":field:`sin` and :field:`sout` are :term:`cumulative counters <cumulative "
"counter>` since boot. Monitor their rate of change rather than the absolute "
"value to detect active :term:`swapping <swap memory>`. On Windows both are "
"always ``0``."
msgstr ""

#: ../../../api.rst:455
msgid ""
">>> import psutil\n"
">>> psutil.swap_memory()\n"
"sswap(total=2097147904, used=886620160, free=1210527744, percent=42.3, "
"sin=1050411008, sout=1906720768)"
msgstr ""

